  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The size of alkali metals increases down the group, so volume also shows increment, and since volume is inversely proportional to the density but in the case <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sr</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ba</mi></math>, increase in the volume is less compared to increasing mass.</p><p>So, down the group density decreases first and then increases.</p><p>Therefore, the&nbsp;correct order of density is as follows:</p><p>&#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ca</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Mg</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Be</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>Sr</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
